# Trivy waivers for THIRD-PARTY images only (the G2 soak gate and any scan of these images).
#
# Separate from .trivyignore on purpose: that file also gates our OWN images in deploy-container.yml,
# and these IDs must not weaken it. Every image below is on the latest upstream tag/digest that exists
# (checked 2026-10-28): the HIGH findings are Go standard library / vendored module versions or
# packages inside the image that upstream has not re-released with fixes yet, or that our scripts never load.
# Our images (node, matcher, caddy-ratelimit, scanner, admin, data-service, bps, websocket) take NO entries.
# Each bump PR re-scans; an ID is removed as soon as a fixed image exists. Review no later than 2026-11-11.
# Usage: trivy image --scanners vuln --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed --ignorefile .trivyignore.thirdparty <ref>

